# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever happens to be committing.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Git-for-Windows default, and without this file it
# is the only thing standing between a Windows editor and a CRLF blob. That is
# not hypothetical here: a whole-file rewrite of diff.mjs reached a commit as
# "300 insertions, 293 deletions" for what was a twelve-line change, because an
# agent rewrote the file and the working copy's CRLF went in with it. A diff
# nobody can read is a change nobody can review, which is most of what this
# repository's pull requests are for.
#
# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository. Working copies still get
# whatever the platform wants on checkout; only the stored bytes are pinned.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images are binary. `text=auto` would usually detect that, but saying so costs
# one line and removes the guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
